 r←ReserveRetrySP n;i;got
⍝ Reserve n seats, each needing both 'SEATS' and 'PAYMENT'. To avoid the deadlock this
⍝ uses non-blocking holds (:Hold … :Else): take 'SEATS', try 'PAYMENT' without waiting,
⍝ and on a miss release everything and retry. It never blocks, so it never deadlocks.
⍝ Each finished booking bumps the shared DONE counter.
⍝ TODO: paired with ReserveRetryPS (opposite order), the two collide every round and
⍝ retry forever. Nothing errors, and nothing progresses.
 :For i :In ⍳n
     got←0
     :Repeat
         :Hold 'SEATS'
             {}⎕DL 0.002        ⍝ (widen the race) let the other flow take its first lock
             :Hold 'PAYMENT'
                 got←1
             :Else
             :EndHold
         :Else
         :EndHold
     :Until got
     :Hold 'DONE' ⋄ DONE+←1 ⋄ :EndHold
 :EndFor
 r←0
